==Serbo-Croatian==

===Etymology===
{{bor+|sh|ota|بره|tr=bre}}, from {{bor|sh|el|μωρέ}}. {{doublet|sh|mȏre}}.

===Interjection===
{{sh-interjection}}

# {{lb|sh|Serbia|colloquial}} {{non-gloss|used to insist on or emphasize something being said or commanded, often also stressing the speaker’s perception of evidentness of the thing insisted on:}} [[bro]], [[man]], [[I say]], I’m [[tell]]ing you, can’t you [[see]]
# {{lb|sh|Serbia|colloquial}} {{non-gloss|used to insist on an answer to or emphasize a question:}} [[on earth]], [[the hell]]
#: {{ux|sh|Šta si '''bre''' to uradio!?|inline=1|What '''the hell''' did you just do!?}}
# {{lb|sh|Serbia|colloquial}} {{non-gloss|used to intensify a preceding interjection}}

====Usage notes====
When marking a statement or question as insistent, {{m|sh||bre}} is ordinarily found either immediately after the verb or at the end of the sentence. However, if an interjection or vocative is present, it can instead appear next to it, following an interjection and following or preceding a vocative. In [[wh-question]]s {{m|sh||bre}} can also follow the interrogative pronoun.

Bre is also used in sentences in a similar way to "bro" in English.

====Related terms====
* {{l|sh|bwe}}

